{
  "_about": "Expected results for the image-based edge cases. NOT ground truth -- these cases are deliberately excluded from data/ground_truth.json and from the benchmark gate. 'raw' is what a perfect extractor should read off the image, with handwriting taking precedence over a struck-through printed value. 'normalised', 'comparison' and 'status' are produced by running those raws through app/engines/normalize.py and compare.py.",
  "_fields": [
    "shipper",
    "consignee",
    "notify_party",
    "port_of_loading",
    "port_of_discharge",
    "container_count",
    "gross_weight_kg"
  ],
  "_inputs": {
    "text_path": "inbox/edge_00N.json -> attachments/*.txt (label parser + LLM fill)",
    "vlm_path": "inbox/edge_00N_scan.json -> scans/*.pdf, image-only PDFs of the crops. read_text() raises UnreadableDocument on them, so extract() takes the _read_visually() fallback.",
    "crops": "images/edge_00N_{email,SI,BL}.png -- the panels on their own, for feeding a model directly."
  },
  "_known_pipeline_gaps": [
    "docs.py _LABEL_LINE requires a label to start with [A-Za-z]. Every bilingual label written CJK-first ('发货人 / Shipper:') therefore fails to match, and the deterministic parser returns NOTHING at all for the Chinese and handwritten-bilingual documents (edge_002, 005, 006). Those cases fall through to the model on every field.",
    "normalize.norm_entity() and norm_port() strip all non-Latin characters, so a value printed only in Chinese normalises to None and is reported absent rather than compared.",
    "normalize.norm_containers() needs a leading digit, so a count spelled out in words ('THREE (3) X 40HQ', edge_005) normalises to None."
  ],
